# Fingerprint-scoped allowances. Each names ONE finding, so any NEW secret in
# these files is still caught — this is not a pattern exemption.
#
# valvebilling/testdata/hash-api-key-vectors.json carries the cross-language
# conformance vectors for hashApiKey. Two of its eight keys are 35 characters
# beginning "vk_", which is the real key prefix, so the scanner reads them as
# credentials. They are synthetic: the file was generated in the monorepo
# specifically as a shareable fixture, its own `note` field records that no
# production pepper or API key appears in it, and the request that produced it
# asked for synthetic values on exactly these grounds. Redis key names leak
# through SCAN, MONITOR and RDB backups — a real key was exposed that way on
# 2026-08-02 — which is why this is the one fixture worth being sure about.
#
# If either vector ever turns out to be real, delete the fixture from both
# repositories, rotate the key, and remove these two lines.
valvebilling/testdata/hash-api-key-vectors.json:generic-api-key:17
valvebilling/testdata/hash-api-key-vectors.json:generic-api-key:66
